# Local env files
#
# `.env.*` is a catch-all so a new per-environment file (e.g. .env.staging, .env.live) can
# never be committed by accident. The negations below MUST stay after it, otherwise the
# committed templates get ignored too.
.env*.local
.env
.env.production
.env.*
!.env.example
!backend/.env.example
backend/.env

# Vercel
.vercel

# TypeScript
*.tsbuildinfo
next-env.d.ts
